\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {14}{\ignorespaces Run-level convergence exclusions across all experimental conditions and synthetic functions. Rows are grouped by noise level and sorted by regularisation condition and optimiser within each group. A filled circle ($\bullet $) indicates the small model run was excluded; a filled square ($\blacksquare $) indicates the big model run was excluded. Empty cells indicate the run was retained. Exclusions are distributed across functions without strong systematic concentration, suggesting non-convergence is driven by experimental conditions rather than function-specific properties.}}{26}{figure.14}\protected@file@percent }
